        <section id="what-is-user-access-control?"  class="t-bg-primary">
          
            <h2>What is user access control?</h2>
              <p>UAC works by requiring a standard user to enter the credentials of an administrator with elevated privileges in order to do high-risk actions like installing a piece of software. This means that standard users cannot install things and therefore reduces the likelihood of them accidentally clicking a link and installing malware.
It’s important therefore that users are not given administration access by default, and that administrators are not logged in with their administrator account when doing day-to-day things such as browsing the internet and checking emails.</p>

          
        </section>
        
    
     
    
  
  
